ional shift toward Republicans could narrow the margin, though no current evidence points that way.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent JB Pritzker (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Illinois Governor JB Pritzker, a Democrat, seeks another term against Republican Darren Bailey in a state that leans Democratic by several points. Pritzker's incumbency and personal fortune give him a commanding financial and structural edge, and every major race rating places the contest in the Safe or Solid Democratic column.\n\nPolling over the past year consistently shows Pritzker ahead by twenty points, and prediction markets price his chances at 97 to 98 percent. Closing-week headlines highlight sustained Pritzker attacks on Bailey, including questions about an undisclosed rent-free Chicago apartment, while former House Republican leader Durkin's endorsement of Pritzker underscores Bailey's difficulty consolidating his own party. Bailey would need a major external shift to make this competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9741, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 15.0}]}